# FTC Challenge Solver & Grading Auditor

## Role

You have two jobs when working in this project:

1. **Solve challenges correctly** — produce code that passes the real grading stack (syntax + universal + per-challenge checks in `codeValidator.ts`).
2. **Audit and report bugs** — when asked to inspect the grading / compiler system, report every known issue clearly and do NOT change any code unless explicitly told to.

---

## How the Grader Actually Works

There is **no real Java compiler**. Grading is static regex/function pattern-matching on source text.

### Grade pipeline

```
checkSyntax()       → any severity:"error" → grade = "wrong"
UNIVERSAL checks    → required fail → "wrong"; improvement fail → caps at "needs-improvement"
CHALLENGE_CHECKS[id]→ per-challenge required/improvement rules (only 19/53 challenges have these)
```

### Three grades

| Grade | Condition |
|---|---|
| `"good"` | All required + all improvement checks pass → triggers auto-complete |
| `"needs-improvement"` | All required pass, ≥1 improvement fails |
| `"wrong"` | ≥1 required check fails OR syntax error |

### Key files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `src/data/challenges.ts` | 53 challenge definitions (narrative + starter code only) |
| `src/lib/codeValidator.ts` | All grading logic (`UNIVERSAL`, `CHALLENGE_CHECKS`, `gradeCode`) |
| `src/components/ChallengeWorkspace.tsx` | Submit flow + check-status display |

---

## Solving Challenges — What the Grader Actually Requires

To reach `"good"`, code must pass **every** universal required + per-challenge required + per-challenge improvement check.

### Universal required (must be present in all submissions)

- `extends LinearOpMode`
- `public void runOpMode()`
- `waitForStart()` present (not inside the loop, not called twice)
- `setTargetPosition(...)` before `setMode(RUN_TO_POSITION)` when using encoders
- No `while(true)` (use `while (opModeIsActive())`)
- No `Thread.sleep()` (use `sleep()`)

### Universal improvement (must pass for `"good"`)

- `telemetry.update()` inside loop when `addData` is used
- `setPower(0)` after encoder/busy-wait move
- Motor not powered without encoder reset before `RUN_TO_POSITION`
- No leftover `// TODO` comments (checked on raw source via `checkOriginal: true`)

### Per-challenge checks (only IDs 1–8, 10, 11, 17, 22, 23, 24, 28, 33, 49, 51, 53)

Read `CHALLENGE_CHECKS[challengeId]` in `codeValidator.ts` before writing code for those IDs. For all other IDs (9, 12–16, 18–21, 25–27, 29–32, 34–48, 50, 52), only universal checks apply — a clean `LinearOpMode` skeleton plus challenge-appropriate logic is enough.

### Syntax rules the checker enforces

- Balanced `{}` and `()`
- No unclosed string literals
- No duplicate variable declarations
- No obvious SDK typos (e.g. `getRunTime`, `SetPower`, `dcmotor.class`)
- ≥3 leftover `// TODO` blocks → forced `"wrong"`

