## Audit Mode — Known Bugs to Report (No Code Changes)

When asked to audit, inspect, or diagnose the grading system, report the following confirmed issues **in plain language**. Do NOT edit any file.

### 1. Coverage gap — 34/53 challenges are ungraded

Challenges **9, 12–16, 18–21, 25–27, 29–32, 34–48, 50, 52** have no `CHALLENGE_CHECKS` entry. Any minimal valid `LinearOpMode` skeleton can score `"good"` without implementing the stated objectives.

### 2. UI requirements list is miswired

`ChallengeWorkspace.tsx` maps `challenge.objectives` to `checkStatuses`, but statuses are keyed by **validator label strings** (e.g. `"DcMotor declared"`), not objective text. The index-fallback `checkStatuses[Object.keys(checkStatuses)[i]]` means the colored pass/fail dots on the left panel are unreliable for most challenges.

### 3. Challenge 6 — "Both motors" check only requires one

The pattern `/\bDcMotor(Ex)?\b/` matches a single occurrence. A student who declares one motor satisfies the check labelled "Both motors declared."

### 4. Challenge 5 (Pedro Pathing) — incomplete path checks

Instructions require `BezierLine` + 3-leg chain. The validator only checks for one `BezierCurve` occurrence. `BezierLine` is not verified, nor is 3-leg count.

### 5. Challenge 22 — `RUN_USING_ENCODER` is `improvement`, not `required`

The FTC review rule (rule #41) and FTC best practice require `RUN_USING_ENCODER` before `setVelocity()`. In `CHALLENGE_CHECKS[22]` it is tier `"improvement"`, so code that calls `setVelocity()` without the mode still passes as `"needs-improvement"`.

### 6. Challenge 23 — wrong sign in P-controller passes

The validator requires `error` and `Kp * error` but never checks `target - current` sign convention. A student using `current - target` (wrong direction, motor fights itself) still gets `"good"`.

### 7. Challenge 7 — servo anti-pattern check passes vacuously

The `shouldBeAbsent` function for "No `setPower` on Servo" returns `false` (absent = good) whenever the word `Servo` is not in the code. A student who never declares a `Servo` bypasses the check.

### 8. Mentor / static ID collision

Static challenges occupy IDs 1–53. If a mentor creates a Supabase challenge whose numeric ID falls in that range, `getChallengeById` in `[id]/page.tsx` prefers the static entry — the mentor challenge never loads.

### 9. Mark Complete bypasses grader

`MarkCompleteButton` writes to localStorage directly with no grader call. Students can mark any challenge complete without submitting code.

### 10. Challenge 8 content — duplicate wording

The instructions say CRServo uses `setPower()` "instead of `setPower()`" (same method name on both sides of the comparison). The hardware name `"diddler_servo"` in starter code and validator tip is inconsistent with typical FTC naming conventions.

